## What landed

**`AdBlockRule`** — structured option parser replacing string-compare matching:
- Type masks against `QWebEngineUrlRequestInfo::resourceType` (incl. `~` inverse + legacy aliases `background`, `object-subrequest`, `xbl`, `dtd`), `third-party`/`first-party` via `firstPartyUrl` host, `domain=`, `denyallow=`, `important`, `badfilter`, `match-case`, `elemhide`/`generichide`/`genericblock`/`document` unbreak flags, `redirect`/`redirect-rule`, `removeparam` (name/`*`/`/re/` subset)
- Unimplementable options (`csp`, `rewrite=`, `header=`, `replace=`, `cookie=`, `sitekey`, `webrtc`, `popup`, `mp4`) render the rule inert rather than misapply it
- Cosmetic markers `##`, `#@#`, `#?#`, `#@?#`, `#$#`, `#@$#`, `##+js()`, `$$` classified distinctly from network rules

**`AdBlockNetwork::match()`** — returns an `AdBlockDecision` (Allow/Block/Redirect + params to strip) evaluated on the IO-thread snapshot; keeps exception-beats-block ordering, `$important` overrides plain exceptions, `$document`/`$genericblock` honored. **`AdBlockRequestInterceptor`** applies it via `block()`, `redirect()`, and query-stripping redirect for removeparam.

**`arora-resource://`** — new scheme + handler serving stub resources (1x1.gif, transparent PNGs, noop.js/txt/html/css, click2load.html, VAST 2–4, VMAP) with uBO/ABP alias normalization.

**Cosmetic engine** — `:-abp-has*` → native `:has()`; procedural ops (`:has-text`, `:matches-css`, `:style`, `:remove*`, `:upward`, `min-text-length`) via injected JS; `+js` scriptlet subset (`set-constant`, `abort-on-property-read/write`, `hide-if-contains`, `remove-class`); exception markers honored.

**Defaults** — now live: EasyList + EasyPrivacy (easylist.to) and uBlock `filters.txt` (uAssets); dead-host stored subscriptions migrate automatically.

## Bugs fixed along the way

- `QUrlQuery::PrettyDecoded` leaves `%3A%2F` encoded in Qt6 — all subscription locations were parsing scheme-less (`Protocol "" is unknown`). Switched to `FullyDecoded` in both `parseUrl` and the migration path.
- Subscription cache writes didn't truncate; in-flight downloads could finish during teardown → `aboutToQuit` now aborts pending replies (this was the intermittent exit segfault).

## Verified

Clean `qmake6 + make` with **0 warnings**; standalone `tst_adblockrule` **120/120**; `--adblock-smoke` PASS; **`--adblock-list-smoke` PASS** — live EasyList download: 79,837 rules, 24,632 cosmetic, rule-derived match + second-subscription match; all prior smokes (`quit-after-load`, `nam`, `history`, `cookie`, `bookmarks`, `search`) exit 0 offscreen.

