## What happened

The previous run was killed mid-task (rc=143 timeout) with the suite mostly ported but uncommitted. I picked it up, verified the infrastructure was in place (`make check` target, rewritten `runTests.sh`, `QT += testlib`, `QAbstractItemModelTester` shim replacing the vendored ModelTest), then chased the remaining failures:

**Real application bugs found by the tests:**
- `AdBlockManager::load()` appended stored subscriptions unconditionally — the custom-rules subscription (created on demand before `load()` runs) got duplicated. Now dedupes by `location()`.
- `AdBlockSubscription::parseUrl` read `lastUpdate` with `PrettyDecoded`, leaving `%3A` in ISO timestamps — now `FullyDecoded`.
- `DownloadItem::saveFileName` only deduped names against files on disk — two parallel downloads to the same suggested name could overwrite each other. Now also checks names claimed by sibling items.

**Test-side determinism:**
- `cleanupButton`'s stalled-HTTP fixture never produced a row: Chromium only emits `downloadRequested` once response *body* bytes arrive — headers alone (or headers+body in one burst) never trigger it. The server now trickles bytes so the download stays in-flight. Verified against a minimal reproducer.
- `opensearchmanager::keywords()` selected engines via `allEnginesNames().at(N)` — Qt6 `QHash::keys()` order varies with insertion history between manager instances. Now selects by sorted name.

**Verification:** `make check` runs 27 test programs offscreen — all pass, 0 failures (the 12 remaining skips are pre-existing unimplemented stubs or QSKIP'd WebKit-only APIs; the two proxy test trees are reported as not-in-build since MIG04 deleted those modules). Committed with the row marked `done`, ChangeLog section added, WORKLOG appended.

