**What shipped**

- `WebPermissionManager` (`src/webpermissionmanager.{h,cpp}`): default-deny broker wired to `QWebEnginePage::permissionRequested`. Notifications/geolocation/mouse-lock get a modal consent prompt naming origin + feature (Deny default, opt-in "Remember this decision"); media capture, screen capture, clipboard, local fonts, and unknown types are denied outright. Requests are serialized through a queue with a re-entrancy guard so bursts can't stack dialogs.
