## Summary

**SEC10 — Rich-text injection via page-controlled strings**: `done`

Centralized defense in `src/utils/safetext.h`:
- `SafeText::escaped()` — for AutoText sinks (tooltips, message boxes). Escaping alone proved insufficient: `Qt::mightBeRichText` doesn't flag `&amp;`/`&quot;`, so the helper wraps escaped text in `<qt>…</qt>` to force the rich renderer to decode entities back to literal characters.
- `SafeText::menu()` — for action/menu text: `&` → `&&` (kills mnemonic injection), `\t`/`\n` stripped (kills fake shortcut columns).
- `PlainTextItemDelegate` — installed on every view fed web-controlled models (EditTreeView/EditTableView, history completer popup, suggestion completer, add-bookmark tree, settings trees).

Sinks hardened: tab labels/tooltips (was double-buggy — showed `&&` literally *and* rendered markup), back/forward + recently-closed menus, ModelMenu/ModelToolBar, download labels + security warning, Add Search Engine / external-app / abp:subscribe prompts (now `Qt::PlainText`), suggestion completer, opensearch/useragent menus, settings tooltips. Engine lookups moved to `QAction::data()` so display text stays presentational.

**Verification**: clean build, `-Wall -Wextra` zero warnings; `tst_safetext` 23/23 offscreen including e2e page titled `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>&more` → literal tab label/tooltip; `make check` 47 programs, 0 failures. Task row, ChangeLog, WORKLOG updated; committed + pushed.
