**What was done:**
- **Audit:** Qt 6.11.3 `QWebEngineProfile` exposes no DOM-storage API — only `clearHttpCache`, `clear*VisitedLinks`, and `cookieStore()->deleteAllCookies()`. Verified the real on-disk layout with a live probe (`Local Storage`, `Session Storage`, `IndexedDB`, `Service Worker`, `WebStorage`, `Trust Tokens`, etc. — all written 0700/0600 by Chromium).
- **`BrowserProfile::clearSiteStorage()`** removes the per-origin storage trees under `persistentStoragePath()`, including Trust Tokens/DIPS/persisted HSTS (`Network Persistent State`).
- **`BrowserProfile::ensureUserOnlyPermissions()`** recursively enforces 0700 dirs / 0600 files (never follows symlinks), run at startup via `applySettings` and after each wipe.
- **`ClearPrivateData`** gained a "Site Data" checkbox (default on, `siteData` QSettings key). Before the filesystem wipe it runs a JS sweep on every open page of the profile (`localStorage`/`sessionStorage.clear()`, `indexedDB.deleteDatabase`, service-worker unregister, `caches.delete`) so Chromium's in-memory StorageAreas can't re-flush stale data.
- **Tests:** `tst_dialogs::clearSiteData` — real e2e: loopback HTTP page seeds localStorage+IndexedDB+cookie on the real "arora" profile, waits for the leveldb commit, then after `accept()` the seeded value is gone from the live page, a fresh same-origin page, and every file on disk; `storagePermissions` verifies 0755/0644 → 0700/0600 repair.

