## Summary

**What was added** — a libFuzzer harness (`fuzz/`) covering every parser that consumes hostile input, built with clang `-fsanitize=fuzzer,address,undefined`:

| Target | Exercises |
|---|---|
| `fuzz_adblockrule` | AdBlock rule syntax incl. `/regex/` rules |
| `fuzz_opensearchreader` | OpenSearch XML (1 MiB cap, DTD rejection) |
| `fuzz_xbel` | XBEL reader → walk → writer → reparse round-trip |
| `fuzz_historyformat` | Serialized history file decode |
| `fuzz_cookiejarstate` | `NetworkCookieJar::restoreState` blobs |
| `fuzz_streamingutils` | `readBoundedList()` hostile count prefixes |
| `fuzz_securestore` | Sealed-blob open + tamper rejection |
| `fuzz_htmltoxbel` | Netscape-bookmark HTML converter |

**Production-code extractions** so fuzzers drive real code:
- `HistoryManager::load()` decode → new `src/history/historyparser.{h,cpp}`
- htmlToXBel `main()` conversion core → `tools/htmlToXBel/converter.{h,cpp}`

**Infrastructure**: seed corpora (~1100 coverage-minimal files), 3 dictionaries, `fuzz/seedgen` for binary formats, `.devin/run-fuzz.sh`, top-level `make check-fuzz` (opt-in; `make check` untouched).

**Verification**: 60s/target × 8 targets, ~7.7M execs — **zero findings in the parsers themselves**. The only two bugs found were in my own drivers (signed-char index in securestore, unopened QBuffer in xbel) — both fixed and re-verified clean. Full build + `make check` (47 test programs) green offscreen.

