## What changed

- **`src/src.pri`** — pinned the deprecation warnings per compiler family via CONFIG scopes: gcc gets `-Wdeprecated -Wdeprecated-declarations`, clang gets `-Wdeprecated-warnings -Wdeprecated-declarations` (clang spec also sets `CONFIG+=gcc`, so clang must be tested first). `warn_on`'s `-Wall -Wextra` stays; no `-Werror` shipped.
