## What was done

**Measured** (headless `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen` via new `--perf-smoke` flag):

| Metric | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Cold start (`app-ctor`) | 6811 ms | 615 ms |
| Adblock setup inside it | 6713 ms | ~599 ms |
| First window | — | 20 ms |
| Tab-open | — | 0.3 ms avg |
| 40k-entry history load | — | ~110 ms |
| 5k-file permission sweep | — | ~20 ms |

**Root cause of the startup stall:** `AdBlockRule` eagerly compiled a `QRegularExpression` for every parsed filter — ~80k PCRE2 compiles (~3s measured standalone for one list) plus 5 helper-regexp recompiles per filter in `convertPatternToRegExp`.

**Fixes:**
- `adblockrule.cpp/.h` — regexp compilation deferred to first `networkMatch` through a shared, mutex-guarded pattern cache. A per-object lazy flag would race: snapshot rules are read on the WebEngine IO thread and GUI thread under read locks. Match semantics unchanged — the PERF02 token index pre-filters, so only rules that actually fire ever compile.
- `historyparser.cpp` — append + single reverse instead of per-entry `QList::prepend` (quadratic under Qt6's contiguous QList).
- `browserprofile.cpp` — SEC12 recursive permission walk deduped to once per profile per launch; chmod only when permissions differ.
- `main.cpp` — permanent `--perf-smoke` harness (test-mode data paths, env-tunable sizes).
- Temporary `PERFDBG` instrumentation removed.

**Verification:** clean qmake+make, `make check` green offscreen (one pre-existing flaky `tst_safetext` data-URL title test — passes on rerun, unrelated), all 196 adblock + history tests pass, zero-warning gate PASS.
